From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 07:58:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Virtual clock stands still while the GE thread draws; texture
 stats line; menu freeze check inside the pause

* Kernel::wait_host(..., zero_time): with the virtual clock a thread waiting for the GE thread (frames in flight, sceGeListSync/DrawSync) no
  longer lets the clock jump by the real time the GE thread needs. Threaded and non-threaded desktop runs now see the same emulated time at the
  same flip (scripted live runs are reproducible, 3 menu openings gave identical times in both modes). Realtime clock (Vita) is unchanged.
* GlSettings::stats_every (gl_stats_every, Vita default 1800 flips): one compact line with the texture cache and HD residency numbers.
* hle_media: the "emulated clock moved while the menu was open" check reads the clock after the pause scope is taken.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

